=== REASONING ===
1. Three domain-specific continuous aggregates needed:
   - cagg_vehicle_daily: fleet overview — battery_level, odometer, speed, temp (1-day bucket)
   - cagg_climate_hourly: climate trends — inside/outside temp, HVAC state, defrost (1-hour bucket)
   - cagg_battery_daily: degradation tracking — min/max/end SoC, pack voltage, charge count (1-day bucket)

2. All use FILTER (WHERE signal = '...') to pivot the EAV signal_log rows into named columns.
   TimescaleDB supports FILTER clauses in continuous aggregate definitions.

3. All created WITH NO DATA — populated lazily by refresh policies, not at creation time.

4. Refresh policies:
   - cagg_vehicle_daily: hourly refresh, 3-day lookback, 1-hour lag
   - cagg_climate_hourly: 30-min refresh, 2-day lookback, 1-hour lag
   - cagg_battery_daily: hourly refresh, 3-day lookback, 1-hour lag

5. Down migration drops all 3 views (CASCADE also removes policies).

6. These complement the existing cagg_signal_hourly (general-purpose) with
   domain-specific pivoted views optimized for frontend page queries.

